-- Per-skill/spell help topics (user 2026-07-18: "also no spell
-- helpfiles? that was my instruction. help files for all skills/spells
-- along with required components" -- a correction: the earlier
-- inline-note-in-`skills` approach was NOT what was asked for, this
-- generates a real `help <name>` topic for every entry in skill.c's
-- SKILLS[] roster instead). Machine-generated -- a one-shot Python
-- script (not committed to the repo; regenerate by hand if skill.c's
-- roster changes significantly) parsed SKILLS[]'s own
-- name/class/tier/level/description fields directly, so this can't
-- drift out of sync with the roster by hand-transcription error.
-- One row per unique skill/spell NAME (25 names are shared across more
-- than one class -- mostly identical weapon-proficiency rows, plus a
-- handful of same-named Cleric/Druid prayers-and-spells like "cure
-- poison" -- merged into a single topic listing every class/tier/level
-- that has it, rather than colliding on help_topic's `name` primary
-- key). Each entry's `Requires:` footer line (new convention, see
-- cmd_help.c's extract_trailing_directive()) names what `cast`/`pray`
-- actually needs on hand for that specific spell -- a spell component
-- (Mage/Druid), a holy symbol (Cleric), the real command it already
-- routes through instead (Thief's `settrap`/`disarmtrap`), or an honest
-- "not yet wired to a command" for the many still-placeholder physical
-- skills (Warrior/Thief/Monk's SKILL_TIER_COMBAT rows and most of their
-- SKILL_TIER_CLASS/ADVANCED ones too -- only `cast`/`pray`-reachable
-- entries, plus set/disarm trap, have a real mechanic as of this
-- session). "disease" is deliberately EXCLUDED here -- it collides with
-- an existing general-mechanic topic (drink a puddle -> catch a disease
-- -- see below) that predates this session's Cleric "disease" prayer;
-- handled by hand-appending to that existing topic instead of fighting
-- over one name.
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE `name` = `name`;

-- "riding" (Mount / riding system, Sneezy → Tobin feature audit)
-- postdates the one-shot generator run above -- hand-added in the same
-- format so it doesn't stand out as a placeholder (the exact class of
-- bug fixed earlier this session, "wiznews/spell help placeholder
-- text"). Deviates from the fixed "Related: skills practice cast pray
-- affects" footer every generated row above shares -- riding has its
-- own real dedicated command pair, not a cast/pray route, so the
-- Related line names those instead.
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE `name` = `name`;
